==English==
[[Image:Langur at Cheri Goemba.jpg|thumb|Gray langur]]

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|inc-hnd}} {{m|ur|لنگور|tr=-}} / {{m|hi|लंगूर|t=monkey}}, from {{der|en|sa|लाङ्गूल|t=tail}} (compare {{m|sa|लाङ्गूलिन्|t=tailed; monkey}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/lʌŋˈɡʊəɹ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-langur.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of the [[Old World]] monkeys of the subfamily {{taxfmt|Colobinae|subfamily}}, in the genera {{taxfmt|Simias|genus}}, {{taxfmt|Trachypithecus|genus}} ([[lutung]]s), {{taxfmt|Presbytis|genus}} ([[surili]]s), and {{taxfmt|Semnopithecus|genus}} ([[gray langur]]s).
# A [[gibbon]] of the genus {{taxfmt|Hoolock|genus}}.

====Derived terms====
